Within a year, Lotus was worth $150 million.

01:16:09.730 --> 01:16:12.730
Wham bam thank you IBM!

01:16:12.730 --> 01:16:15.730
Time to walk down the road!

01:16:17.730 --> 01:16:21.730
IBM had forecast sales of half a million computers by 1984.

01:16:21.730 --> 01:16:25.730
In those three years, they sold 2 million.

01:16:25.730 --> 01:16:26.730
Yeah!

01:16:26.730 --> 01:16:29.730
Euphoric, I guess is the right word.

01:16:29.730 --> 01:16:33.730
Everybody believed that they were not going to...

01:16:33.730 --> 01:16:36.730
At that point, 2 million or 3 million,

01:16:36.730 --> 01:16:38.730
they were now thinking in terms of 100 million.

01:16:38.730 --> 01:16:41.730
They were probably off the scale in the other direction.

01:16:41.730 --> 01:16:45.460
What did all this mean to Bill Gates,

01:16:45.460 --> 01:16:49.460
whose operating system DOS was at the heart of every IBM PC sold?

01:16:49.460 --> 01:16:55.460
sold? Initially not much because of the deal with IBM, but it did give him a vital bridgehead

